 "What are the like terms in the expression $3h-v+7u+3t+5x?$" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(3h)+(-v)+(7u)+(3t)+(5x).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48b07f47-4fcc-58ea-be39-752a6cbb826f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48b07f47-4fcc-58ea-be39-752a6cbb826f" :answer-field/id #uuid "48b07f47-4fcc-58ea-be39-752a6cbb826f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-903c3f02-1d63-5d7e-99c2-58db15363a93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f33585fa-e18e-59b6-b2e0-40aeaf074f86" "answer-b09bec20-e545-5d14-b9cb-fde4bc352f4c" "answer-a1b10e45-7174-511f-99e5-751845ff6f99" "answer-a40eed80-a657-531e-9e30-b6272fd74f47" "answer-903c3f02-1d63-5d7e-99c2-58db15363a93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f33585fa-e18e-59b6-b2e0-40aeaf074f86" :answer/id #uuid "f33585fa-e18e-59b6-b2e0-40aeaf074f86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-v$, $7u$ and $3h$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09bec20-e545-5d14-b9cb-fde4bc352f4c" :answer/id #uuid "b09bec20-e545-5d14-b9cb-fde4bc352f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3h$ and $3t$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1b10e45-7174-511f-99e5-751845ff6f99" :answer/id #uuid "a1b10e45-7174-511f-99e5-751845ff6f99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3h$ and $7u$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a40eed80-a657-531e-9e30-b6272fd74f47" :answer/id #uuid "a40eed80-a657-531e-9e30-b6272fd74f47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5x$ and $3t$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-903c3f02-1d63-5d7e-99c2-58db15363a93" :answer/id #uuid "903c3f02-1d63-5d7e-99c2-58db15363a93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No like  terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d0f76c69-d8c0-5996-bfc8-0e524b6847e9" :question/id #uuid "d0f76c69-d8c0-5996-bfc8-0e524b6847e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101748" :question/problem "What are the like terms in the expression $8x-9y+10z+8$" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(8x)+(-9y)+(10z)+(8).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc72e96b-988d-51c4-90d2-308f4675a55c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc72e96b-988d-51c4-90d2-308f4675a55c" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc72e96b-988d-51c4-90d2-308f4675a55c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d151fce3-aa5a-521b-8fbd-d23441da29ab" "answer-5baf360d-8b56-5d04-b7a0-1a1d7685f8d3" "answer-5b86a1e1-1879-52ac-9479-2f1729eb4348" "answer-be98f75a-60d7-5ace-9fcc-ffa5487165d9" "answer-05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d151fce3-aa5a-521b-8fbd-d23441da29ab" :answer/id #uuid "d151fce3-aa5a-521b-8fbd-d23441da29ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-9y$ and $10z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5baf360d-8b56-5d04-b7a0-1a1d7685f8d3" :answer/id #uuid "5baf360d-8b56-5d04-b7a0-1a1d7685f8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-9y$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b86a1e1-1879-52ac-9479-2f1729eb4348" :answer/id #uuid "5b86a1e1-1879-52ac-9479-2f1729eb4348" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8x$ and $10z$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be98f75a-60d7-5ace-9fcc-ffa5487165d9" :answer/id #uuid "be98f75a-60d7-5ace-9fcc-ffa5487165d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8x$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0" :answer/id #uuid "05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No like terms" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aaf35c78-310f-5644-af7b-d8eed5daf52f" :question/id #uuid "aaf35c78-310f-5644-af7b-d8eed5daf52f" :question/math-academy-id "q-243" :question/problem "How many pairs of like terms are present in the expression $2x-4y+3-7x+10y-5$?" :question/worked-solution "There are three pairs of like terms:  the $x$ terms, the $y$ terms, and the constant terms $3$ and $-5$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fed1a132-6920-5b6c-9601-bce23809d1f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fed1a132-6920-5b6c-9601-bce23809d1f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "fed1a132-6920-5b6c-9601-bce23809d1f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48ec5148-d0ac-5e44-9c3c-ea5a699fe9de" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a6aa7601-2ac6-58ff-8434-3dfa0b950af4" "answer-48ec5148-d0ac-5e44-9c3c-ea5a699fe9de" "answer-1d6fb221-0334-5ada-8a0d-1fcb2eb0fcf8" "answer-133b772f-765b-5463-9238-333375439ba6" "answer-f41c449c-4ba4-534a-9077-4d2964da8876"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6aa7601-2ac6-58ff-8434-3dfa0b950af4" :answer/id #uuid "a6aa7601-2ac6-58ff-8434-3dfa0b950af4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48ec5148-d0ac-5e44-9c3c-ea5a699fe9de" :answer/id #uuid "48ec5148-d0ac-5e44-9c3c-ea5a699fe9de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d6fb221-0334-5ada-8a0d-1fcb2eb0fcf8" :answer/id #uuid "1d6fb221-0334-5ada-8a0d-1fcb2eb0fcf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-133b772f-765b-5463-9238-333375439ba6" :answer/id #uuid "133b772f-765b-5463-9238-333375439ba6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f41c449c-4ba4-534a-9077-4d2964da8876" :answer/id #uuid "f41c449c-4ba4-534a-9077-4d2964da8876" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b4754c7a-8749-5793-bafb-b31cee518a08" :question/id #uuid "b4754c7a-8749-5793-bafb-b31cee518a08" :question/math-academy-id "q-75670" :question/problem "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $6p-3+5q-2p-3q+1?$" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(6p)+(-3)+(5q)+(-2p)+(-3q)+(1)\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $6p$ and $-2p$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $p.$\n\n- $5q$ and $-3q$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $q.$\n\n- $-3$ and $1$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-128088e5-82fb-5590-85f8-009c087cafef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-128088e5-82fb-5590-85f8-009c087cafef" :answer-field/id #uuid "128088e5-82fb-5590-85f8-009c087cafef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3e8bceef-d437-5965-b3f7-06f784fdb2cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-838d51cc-3d11-524b-8c2e-fc03bc3db6de" "answer-1a4d5dde-dec3-5bd0-bc98-11f4d40df504" "answer-f3783601-7d45-507d-ae0a-45c8519419b9" "answer-3e8bceef-d437-5965-b3f7-06f784fdb2cd" "answer-5e91f9b6-ccd1-5956-9d4f-018d30330539"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-838d51cc-3d11-524b-8c2e-fc03bc3db6de" :answer/id #uuid "838d51cc-3d11-524b-8c2e-fc03bc3db6de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a4d5dde-dec3-5bd0-bc98-11f4d40df504" :answer/id #uuid "1a4d5dde-dec3-5bd0-bc98-11f4d40df504" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3783601-7d45-507d-ae0a-45c8519419b9" :answer/id #uuid "f3783601-7d45-507d-ae0a-45c8519419b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e8bceef-d437-5965-b3f7-06f784fdb2cd" :answer/id #uuid "3e8bceef-d437-5965-b3f7-06f784fdb2cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e91f9b6-ccd1-5956-9d4f-018d30330539" :answer/id #uuid "5e91f9b6-ccd1-5956-9d4f-018d30330539" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079135 :question/problem "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $a+2b+3-10b-9-8a?$" :question/worked-solution "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(a)+(2b)+(3)+(-10b)+(-9)+(-8a).\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $a$ and $-8a$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $2b$ and $-10b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n- $3$ and $-9$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186077588 :answer-field/correct 17592186077591 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079609 :tutorial/content "Terms in a linear expression are called **like terms** if their variable part is the same. For example, in the linear expression\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}2x}+3y{\\color{blue}-5x},\n$$\n\nthe terms ${\\color{blue}2x}$ and ${\\color{blue}-5x}$ are like terms because both terms contain the same variable $x.$\n\nA linear expression may also contain multiple groups of like terms. For example, in the expression\n\n$$\n2a + \\dfrac{1}{2}b + 3a - 0.4 b - a,\n$$\n\nwe have two groups of like terms:\n\n- $2a,$ $3a,$ and $-a$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $\\dfrac{1}{2}b$ and $-0.4b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n**Remember:** When a term has a subtraction symbol $(-)$ in front of it, the term is treated as a *negative*." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079628 :tutorial/content "In some expressions, there are no like terms. For example, in the expression \n\n$$\na+2b\n$$\n\n there are two terms, $a$ and $2b$. These two terms do not have the same variable part, so they are not like terms." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078666 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079416 :step/math-academy-id 669614 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079522 :step/math-academy-id 669615 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079523 :step/math-academy-id 669618 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079419 :step/math-academy-id 669619 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079524 :step/math-academy-id 669622 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079418 :step/math-academy-id 669623 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
